### mt76 027: send WLAN_FUNC_SET_WAIT_DEL_STA to the NPU on station teardown so the departing
### wcid's per-TID station bitmap (RRO SRAM) is cleared before the index is reused. Root fix for
### the reconnect offload-death (FOE_ID=0 storm, reboot-only recovery) that blocks running
### bridger/flowtable on the W1700K — for NON-Apple clients. 027's CLEAR does NOT reach the Apple/
### multi-TID poison (confirmed on-device 2026-08-12), so it is paired with 031 (fanboy's reworked 0015
### index-dodge) which covers that case. NOT competing: 027 clears, 031 dodges; run both. Adds a
### function to mt76 only (no airoha_offload.h struct change) → normal mt76 rebuild, no brick concern.
### ABI recovered from iCare's reverse-engineered NPU fw (airoha-npu-fdk, services/wifi): enum
### ordinals match airoha_offload.h, DEL_STA is ifindex=action(0=SET/1=CLEAR/2=QUERY/3=CLEAR_ALL),
### payload=(tid<<11)|(wcid&0x7ff). Patch issues CLEAR (action=1) for TID 0..8 of the wcid (TID max
### is 8 in the NPU fw; 8 = non-QoS/mgmt slot where PMF frames latch — 0..7 alone left it poisoned).
### Verify offload + RX survive client reconnects (esp. macOS/iOS PMF) with bridger enabled.
027-wifi-mt76-mt7996-npu-del-sta-on-teardown.patch:package/kernel/mt76/patches/027-wifi-mt76-mt7996-npu-del-sta-on-teardown.patch

### mt76 031: fanboy's REWORKED 0015 (avoid-stale-npu-wcid-reuse), carried ALONGSIDE 027. 027 CLEARs the
### NPU per-wcid state on teardown but that does NOT reach whatever Apple/multi-TID clients dirty (poison
### CONFIRMED on our own tree 2026-08-12: borrowed iPhone, 6 GHz, HWF stalls to 0 / traffic to CPU / core
### pins; healthy control same band proves it's a real regression). 031 DODGES instead of clears: hands a
### reconnecting station a fresh wcid so it never lands on the poisoned index — structure-agnostic, which is
### why it covers the Apple case where the clear doesn't. Reworked vs the old 0015 time-bomb: (a) only stashes
### clients that ran >1 concurrent RX BA session (rx_ba_tids>1 = iPhone/multi-TID footprint), (b) rotating
### oldest-first recycle when the fresh pool exhausts (needs 1023+ multi-TID assocs/boot to reach = academic).
### Complementary to 027 (027 inserts before mt76_wcid_mask_clear, 031 stashes after) — applies clean on top,
### touches only mt7996.h + main.c (no airoha_offload.h → normal mt76 rebuild). Source: OpenWRT-fanboy/OpenW1700k
### @ubi2. Keep until a proper root fix for the Apple poison lands. See [[project_w1700k_npu_del_sta]].
